---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const repo = 'https://github.com/atarik23/ProjNO_PortOpt_Agic';
const figures = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/atarik23/ProjNO_PortOpt_Agic/main/Docs/Images';
const metrics = [
  { label: 'GMV expected return', value: '0.726733%' },
  { label: 'GMV risk', value: '0.134594%' },
  { label: 'Frontier portfolios', value: '25' },
  { label: 'Dense/sparse max. weight difference', value: '5.551 × 10⁻¹⁷' },
];
---

<Layout title="Mean-Variance Portfolio Optimizer — Tarik Agić">
  <main class="article">
    <a class="back" href="/work">← All projects</a>
    <header class="article-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Numerical Optimization <span>·</span> Academic Project <span>·</span> 2026</p>
      <h1>Mean-Variance Portfolio Optimizer</h1>
      <p class="dek">A C++ portfolio explorer implementing active-set quadratic programming with interchangeable dense and sparse linear-system backends.</p>
      <div class="byline">
        <span>Tarik Agić</span><span class="separator" aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Individual project</span>
      </div>
      <nav class="resources" aria-label="Project resources">
        <a href={repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a>
        <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/Docs/ProjNO_PortOpt_Agic.pdf`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Technical report ↗</a>
        <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/Implementation/README.md`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Documentation ↗</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <article class="body">
      <section aria-labelledby="overview">
        <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
        <p>Developed as an individual project for the <em>Numerical Optimization</em> course, this C++ application constructs long-only portfolios that minimize variance for a selected expected return. It estimates asset-return statistics from validated CSV data and presents the resulting allocations through a native graphical interface built with the professor-provided natID framework.</p>
        <p>The application includes an efficient-frontier explorer, allocation and weight-path visualizations, backend comparison, CSV export, and reproducible synthetic and historical ETF examples.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="implementation">
        <h2 id="implementation">Implementation</h2>
        <p>The optimization problem is formulated as a convex quadratic program with full-investment, target-return, and non-negativity constraints:</p>
        <div class="equation" role="img" aria-label="Minimize one half w transpose Sigma w, subject to mu transpose w equals r, sum of weights equals one, and weights are nonnegative.">min ½ wᵀΣw &nbsp; subject to &nbsp; μᵀw = r, &nbsp; 1ᵀw = 1, &nbsp; w ≥ 0</div>
        <p>I implemented a <strong>feasible primal active-set solver</strong> that solves Karush–Kuhn–Tucker (KKT) systems, updates active zero-weight bounds, and verifies feasibility after convergence. The same optimization algorithm uses either the natID <code>dense::DblMatrix</code> or <code>sparse::DblSolver</code> backend.</p>
        <p>The interface allows target-return selection, displays the efficient frontier and portfolio weights, and compares solutions across backends. The natID matrix libraries and GUI framework were externally provided; the project-specific solver, integration, interface, tests, and report were my work.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="results">
        <h2 id="results">Results</h2>
        <p>On the bundled five-asset synthetic dataset, the application constructed 25 feasible efficient-frontier portfolios. Dense and sparse backends produced numerically matching allocations, and the automated verification suite passed, including correlated 20-asset test cases.</p>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table>
            <caption>Selected results from the reproducible synthetic sample</caption>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Metric</th><th scope="col">Result</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {metrics.map((metric) => <tr><td>{metric.label}</td><td class="numeric">{metric.value}</td></tr>)}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="figures">
          <figure>
            <img src={`${figures}/efficient_frontier.png`} alt="Portfolio Explorer efficient-frontier visualization" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption><strong>Figure 1.</strong> Efficient frontier and selected portfolio in the graphical application.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img src={`${figures}/portfolio_weights.png`} alt="Portfolio weight paths across target returns" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption><strong>Figure 2.</strong> Changes in asset allocation across target returns.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
        <p>The project also includes a documented five-ETF historical sample for demonstration, not investment forecasting or out-of-sample performance evaluation. Additional interface screenshots and numerical checks are available in the <a href={`${repo}/tree/main/Docs/Images`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">repository figures ↗</a> and the <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/Docs/ProjNO_PortOpt_Agic.pdf`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">technical report ↗</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </article>

    <footer class="article-footer">
      <span>C++20 · natID SDK · natGUI · CMake · CTest</span>
      <a href="/work">← Back to work</a>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Layout>

